# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output, scratch, and generated figures.
#
# Everything below is either produced by a script in this repository or
# copied in from the cluster, and none of it is a source. 3,288 untracked
# files were sitting here before this was written, which is enough noise to
# hide a source file that was never committed -- and it did: the whole test
# suite, `integrator.utils.checkpoints`, `integrator.fit`, and four of the
# documents CLAUDE.md points at.
#
# A figure is regenerated by `scripts/figures/render_all.sh` and a table by
# `make_tables.py`, so neither is kept here. The reduced CSV/npz tables they
# read ARE kept, under `docs/figures/data/`, because they come off
# purge-eligible netscratch and a figure cannot be redrawn without them.

# Training output
checkpoints/
lightning_logs/
wandb/
*.ckpt

# Scratch working directories
.scratch_*/
/docs_drafts/

# Figure and evaluation output copied back from the cluster. Anchored with
# a leading slash: an unanchored `data/` also matches `tests/data/`, which
# silently left all 38 test fixtures out of the commit that claimed to
# add them, making the committed suite unrunnable on a clone.
/paper_figures/
/laue_figures/
/finished_figs_local/
/architecture_comparison/
/reference_eval/
# NOT `reference_data/`: that is the R-free flag set, the starting model and
# the refinement eff files -- inputs that every comparable number depends on,
# not output. Ignoring it is why the fixed-flag pair sat untracked while the
# pipeline used the flag-generating one; see docs/reference_data.md.
!reference_data/
!reference_data/**
/friedel_pairs/
/friedel_pairs_9b7c/
/1117_eval/
/data/

# Rendered figures and tables: generated, so not sources
docs/figures/**/*.pdf
docs/figures/**/*.png
docs/figures/**/*.svg
docs/figures/**/*.dot
docs/figures/*.html
docs/tables/
docs/figs/

# One-off files that accumulate at the root
temp.py
temp.txt
arch_glyphs.npz

# Claude Code: the hook and its settings are shared; a stray copy of the
# per-user memory directory is not.
.claude/projects/
.claude/settings.local.json

# One-off scripts and data left at the root. Named rather than matched by a
# pattern, so a real source added here later is not silently ignored.
# Plotting belongs in scripts/figures/ -- see CLAUDE.md, "Figures".
make_arch_diagrams.py
make_arch_glyphs.py
openhermite.py
plot_geom_fallback.py
plot_i.py
plot_profile_grid.py
sim_patch.py
sim.yaml
ragged_data_module.txt
poisson2_*.npz
sbgrid_anomalous_*.csv

# Test fixtures are sources, whatever their extension. `*.log` above is for
# run output, but `tests/data/metrics/` holds real `dials.scale`,
# `dials.merge` and careless logs copied from output, and those are what
# `test_metrics_contract.py` and `test_dials_log.py` read. CLAUDE.md calls
# them the thing that stops the readers drifting; a test that skips or
# errors for a missing fixture pins nothing.
!tests/data/**/*.log
!tests/data/**/*.csv
